# netsurf (vita frontend): downloads fall back to ux0:data/VitaBrowser/downloads/
# Generated 2026-09-30
#
# Hardware run 27, the first device run of the download test: "download:
# cannot create ux0:download/vita-test.bin (errno 2)", interaction 30/31.
# Every VitaBrowser VPK is a safe eboot (frontends/vita/Makefile:
# vita-make-fself -s), and a safe app is kept out of most of ux0:, so
# sceIoMkdir("ux0:/download") fails (its result was not checked) and the
# fopen gets ENOENT. (Not the trailing slash: VitaSDK newlib's mkdir runs
# the path through __realpath, which drops it -- checked by running the
# libc's own __realpath under an emulator: "ux0:download/" ->
# "ux0:/download", the form ux0:data/VitaBrowser/ takes too.) ux0:data/
# is inside the sandbox; log.txt is written there.
#
# - download.c: vita_download_dirs[] = ux0:download/, then
#   ux0:data/VitaBrowser/downloads/; each is made without its trailing
#   slash and checked to be a directory (a failure is logged: "download:
#   cannot make ..."), then the file is opened there. A build that may
#   write ux0:download/ still saves there.
# - chrome.c: the home page lists the files in both folders.
# - interact.c: the download check looks in both folders and names the
#   path it found.
# tools/run-vita-sim.sh now models the sandbox (ux0:download is made a
# plain file), so the simulator takes the device's path and the gate
# checks the fallback file byte for byte.
